      "id": "kasqzep",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Composition of the Atmosphere"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Nitrogen (78%) and Oxygen (21%) make up approximately 99% of the total atmospheric volume.",
        "The Troposphere is the lowest atmospheric layer where virtually all weather phenomena occur.",
        "The Stratosphere contains the vital Ozone layer, which absorbs harmful ultraviolet solar radiation.",
        "The Mesosphere is the coldest layer of the atmosphere where temperature drops to -100°C and meteorites burn up.",
        "The Thermosphere contains the Ionosphere, facilitating global radio communications by reflecting radio waves."
      ],
      "id": "4tqcwll"
    },
